भारण्ड भारण्ड, अस्, m., N. of a fabulous
bird, (also written भारुण्ड, भेरण्ड, भेरुण्ड);
(ई), f. the female of the above bird.

भरीमन्, आ, m., Ved. a household, family;
bearing, supporting, nourishing, cherishing (in this
sense the gender is doubtful).

, a form भर्त्स्यामि occurs), to menace, threaten;
to reproach, abuse, blame, reprove, chide, rebuke; to
deride: Pass. भर्त्स्यते.

भारक, अम्, n. a load, burden, weight, a par-
ticular weight; (अस्, इका, अम्), loaded with, (at the
end of comps.; cf. फणि-भारिका.)

भारिक, अस्, आ, अम्, forming a load, heavy;
swollen (said of a particular kind of elephantiasis);
(अस्), m. a burden-bearer, porter.

भारुण्ड भारुण्ड, अस्, m. = भारण्ड, q. v.;
(अम्), n., N. of a Sāman; of a wood mentioned
in Rāmāyaṇa
